-- title:
--   Complete regular local W₀-algebras of dimension 2 as W₀[[X₀,X₁]]/(π-h)
-- statement:
--   Let $W_0$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain) and let $\pi \in W_0$ be an element generating its maximal ideal, so $\mathfrak{m}_{W_0} = (\pi)$. Let $R$ be a commutative noetherian local ring which is a $W_0$-algebra, complete (and separated) for the adic topology of its maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_R$, regular local, of Krull dimension $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} R = 2$. Assume further that every $r \in R$ satisfies $r - \varphi(w) \in \mathfrak{m}_R$ for some $w \in W_0$, where $\varphi \colon W_0 \to R$ is the structure map (so the residue field of $R$ is generated by the constants), that $\varphi(\pi) \in \mathfrak{m}_R$, and that two given elements $x_0, x_1 \in R$ satisfy $\mathfrak{m}_R = (x_0, x_1)$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a power series $h \in W_0[[X_0,X_1]]$ with vanishing constant coefficient and of an isomorphism of $W_0$-algebras $e \colon R \xrightarrow{\sim} W_0[[X_0,X_1]] / (C(\pi) - h)$, where $C(\pi)$ is the constant power series $\pi$, such that $e(x_0)$ and $e(x_1)$ are the classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$ respectively.
--
--   This is the structure theorem for a complete regular local ring of dimension $2$ over a discrete valuation ring of constants, in the presentation adapted to a chosen pair of generators of the maximal ideal: such a ring is a quotient of a two-variable power series ring over $W_0$ by one relation of the shape $\pi - h$ with $h$ in the maximal ideal. It is used to put a deformation ring, presented by a Drinfeld-type basis, into the normal form $W_0[[X_0,X_1]]/(\pi - h)$.
-- source:
